{
  "content": "<h1><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ImportBankStatement\">Import bank statement</span></h1><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Action Count Download Import On Port To ToDate Transaction\">Most banks allow you to download transaction data for import into accounting systems.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Error Import ImportBankStatement Manual Port Statement To ToDate\">Import bank statements to save time and reduce manual data entry errors.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Import ImportBankStatement Port Statement To ToDate\">How to Import Bank Statements</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account Accounts And BankAndCashAccounts Count On To ToDate\">Navigate to the <strong>Bank and Cash Accounts</strong> tab.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block pointer-events-none ltr:pr-8 rtl:pl-8\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 ltr:pl-8 rtl:pr-8\"><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"border-y ltr:border-l rtl:border-r border-neutral-300 bg-white p-4 flex gap-2 items-center\"><i class=\"fas fa-coins text-neutral-400\"></i><span class=\"font-semibold text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"BankAndCashAccounts\">Bank and Cash Accounts</span></span></div><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Import ImportBankStatement On Port Statement To ToDate\">Click the <strong>Import Bank Statement</strong> button in the bottom-right corner.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pb-4 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 p-3 border-b\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4\"><span class=\"border text-xs rounded py-1 px-2 bg-white border-neutral-300 text-neutral-400\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ImportBankStatement\">Import bank statement</span></span></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Account And Bank_account BankAccount Count Next On Select Statement\">Select the bank account and choose your bank statement file, then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 text-neutral-900 p-8 text-sm\"><span class=\"border font-semibold rounded-md py-3 px-4 bg-[#428bca] border-[#357ebd] text-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Next\">Next</span></span></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action And Balance Count Import On Port Summary To ToDate Transaction View\">Review the import summary showing balances and transaction counts, then click <strong>Import</strong> to proceed.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 text-neutral-900 p-8 text-sm\"><span class=\"border font-semibold rounded-md py-3 px-4 bg-[#428bca] border-[#357ebd] text-white\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Import\">Import</span></span></div></div><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Import Port\">After Import</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action Automatic Create Import On Payment Payments Port Receipt Receipts To ToDate Transaction Transactions\">Imported transactions are automatically created as <em>Receipts</em> or <em>Payments</em>.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action And Automatic BankRules Import On Port To ToDate Transaction Transactions\">Use <em>Bank Rules</em> to automatically categorize imported transactions and save time.</p><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Automatic LearnMore On To ToDate\">Learn more about automatic categorization:</span> <a href=\"/guides/bank-rules\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"BankRules\">Bank Rules</span></a></p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"History Import Is On Port To ToDate Undo\">To undo an import, use the <strong>History</strong> screen to reverse the changes.</p><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action LearnMore On Transaction Transactions\">Learn more about reversing transactions:</span> <a href=\"/guides/history\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"History\">History</span></a></p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Port Support\">Supported File Formats</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Port Statement Support\">Manager supports these bank statement formats:</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"On\">• <strong>Most reliable</strong>: QIF, OFX, QFX, QBO, STA, SWI, 940, IIF, CAMT053, CAMT052</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Less On To ToDate\">• <strong>Less reliable</strong>: XML, CSV (due to non-standard formats)</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"On Port Support\">• <strong>Not supported</strong>: PDF (designed for human reading, not data processing)</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Automatic Column Layout On To ToDate\">Manager automatically interprets various CSV column layouts despite the lack of standardization.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Is On\">Common Issues</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action BankReconciliation BankReconciliations Date Export On Port Reconciliation Transaction Transactions\"><strong>Duplicate transactions</strong> - Usually occur when banks change transaction dates between exports. Regular <em>bank reconciliations</em> help identify duplicates.</p><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"BankReconciliation BankReconciliations LearnMore On Reconciliation\">Learn more about bank reconciliations:</span> <a href=\"/guides/bank-reconciliations\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"BankReconciliations\">Bank Reconciliations</span></a></p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Date DateFormat On Pending\"><strong>Date format confusion</strong> - Dates like 01-02-2024 could mean January 2nd or February 1st depending on format.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action Date DateFormat Import On Port To ToDate Transaction Transactions\">Manager analyzes your file to determine the most likely date format. Import files with many transactions for better accuracy.</p>",
  "key": "import-bank-statement"
}
